-- whose initial value does not meet the annotation.  `0` is not `_ > 0`, and
-- it is the result on `[]`.  The annotation's own obligation is a skip with
-- the base reason (never a violation: the base is data dependent), an error
-- under `cap verified`; it is not assumed in the body, and `s` gets nothing.
-- Before phase 4 this module was rejected too, for `need_pos(s)` (nothing
